-- title:
--   From HTo GPaper Total Error Le
-- statement:
--   **The literal paper telescope error is absorbed by the corrected from-H-to-G envelope.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ be LDT parameters, let $\gamma\ge0$, let $0\le\zeta\le1$, and let $k\in\mathbb N$. Define the literal paper telescope error by
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{paper}}=
--   k\left(2\sqrt{2\zeta}+
--   2\sqrt{426k^2m\left(\gamma^{1/16}+\zeta^{1/16}+(d/q)^{1/16}\right)}\right),
--   $$
--
--   and define the corrected envelope by
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{corr}}=
--   46k^2m\left(\gamma^{1/32}+\zeta^{1/32}+(d/q)^{1/32}\right).
--   $$
--
--   Then the formal inequality is
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{paper}}\le E_{\mathrm{corr}}.
--   $$
--
--   The estimate converts the literal per-step recurrence bound into the quadratic error scale used by the final from-H-to-G comparison theorem.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGPaperTotalError_le`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
